  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "note",
      "type": "note",
      "text": "Cook opt 05 \u2014 SOP cooks\n\nWindow title: \"05 geometry\". Four sheets, left to right, top row then bottom.\nEach sheet is a vertical grid in its own render.\n\n1 NoiseSOP speed 0. A BUMPY sheet that stays STILL.\n2 NoiseSOP speed 1.5. The same kind of bumps, and they KEEP MOVING.\n3 PointSOP expressions px, py, pz. A FLAT sheet that stays STILL.\n4 PointSOP Y = py + sin(t) * 0.45. The sheet BOBS up and down.\n\nAttributeSOP is the same rule as PointSOP: an expression that reads t cooks, a constant does not. There is no separate picture for it, because a point attribute does not move the sheet on its own.\nNoiseVOL has no simple picture in this set.\n\nFail if cell 1 crawls, cell 2 is frozen, cell 3 bobs, cell 4 is frozen, or a cell is an empty background.",
      "position": [
        -40,
        -280
      ],
      "size": [
        720,
        280
      ],
      "color": [
        1.0,
        0.95,
        0.55,
        0.92
      ]
    }
  ]
